From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: dt-platdev: block SM6450

SM6450 scales its CPUs through qcom-cpufreq-hw. Now that the CPUs carry
OPP tables for interconnect scaling, keep cpufreq-dt from registering
for them as well.

---
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
@@ -176,6 +176,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id blocklist[] __initconst = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6150", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375", },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6450", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7125", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7225", },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7325", },
